# Repository-level deterministic line-ending policy.
#
# G-4: canonical governed content is the exact bytes of the checked-out
# canonical source file. That is only deterministic if the checkout
# representation is deterministic, and without an explicit rule it is
# governed by each machine's core.autocrlf. A fresh clone on a host with
# core.autocrlf=true produced CRLF working-tree bytes where this working
# tree has LF, which yields a different content_fingerprint for the same
# source. The policy belongs here, in the repository, rather than hidden
# inside the fingerprint algorithm where it would weaken the meaning of
# the digest.
#
# `text=auto` lets git detect binary content and leave it alone; the 24
# tracked binary files (.png, .pdf, .svg, .wasm, .woff*) are unaffected.
# At the time this rule was added every tracked file was stored with LF in
# the index (i/crlf = 0, i/mixed = 0), so no renormalization was required
# and none was performed.
* text=auto eol=lf